# Python-Specific Rules (sample)

> This file is a sample with the `.example` extension. Activate by copying without the extension:
> ```bash
> cp .claude/rules/language-python.md.example .claude/rules/language-python.md
> ```
>
> Edit to fit your project. Delete sections you don't need.

## Python version

- Python 3.11+ assumed
- Actively use `match`, type parameter syntax, and exception groups
- Use `from __future__ import annotations` when you need deferred evaluation of annotations (e.g. forward references). PEP 563 is being superseded by PEP 649, which changes semantics in Python 3.14+; through Python 3.13 the future-import remains the way to opt into deferred evaluation

## Type hints

- Mandatory on all functions and methods
- Include `-> None` explicitly
- `typing.Any` is forbidden; use `object` or `TypeVar`
- Use builtin generics (`list[int]`, `dict[str, int]`) — 3.9+
- Prefer `T | None` over `Optional[T]` — 3.10+

## Error handling

- Catch specific exceptions (`ValueError`, custom ones); `except Exception` is last resort
- Bare `except:` is forbidden
- Chain exceptions: `raise NewError(...) from original`
- Never swallow exceptions in `finally`

## Naming conventions

- Modules / functions / variables: `snake_case`
- Classes: `PascalCase`
- Constants: `UPPER_SNAKE_CASE`
- Private: `_leading_underscore` (not exported)
- `__double_underscore__` only for special methods

## File organization

- 1 module, 1 responsibility. Consider splitting beyond 500 lines
- `__init__.py` is re-exports only (no side effects)
- Tests live under `tests/` or match `test_*.py`

## Forbidden patterns

- `eval` / `exec` (absolutely forbidden for user-controlled input)
- Global mutable state (module-level `list = []`, etc.)
- Leftover `print` debugging in production (use logger)
- `time.sleep` for test synchronization (use `pytest-asyncio`, `tenacity`)

## Logging

- Standard `logging` module or `structlog` recommended
- Levels: `DEBUG` / `INFO` / `WARNING` / `ERROR` / `CRITICAL`
- Never log PII (personal information)

## Tests

- Standardize on `pytest`
- Setup/teardown via fixtures
- Parameterized: `@pytest.mark.parametrize`
- Async: `@pytest.mark.asyncio`
- Coverage targets follow `project-config.md` §6

## Recommended tools

- `ruff` (lint + format, Black-compatible)
- `mypy` or `pyright` for type checking
- `uv` / `pip-tools` / `poetry` for dependency management

## Dependency packages

- Record new additions in `project-config.md` §2
- Vulnerability scanning: `pip-audit` / `safety` run periodically (automated via `/security-scan` skill)

## Concept alignment

- Project-wide conventions live in `project-config.md` §2 / §6
- This file contains Python-specific details only
